        <mxCell id="c171" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#B85450;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c49" target="c170"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c172" value="&lt;b&gt;PS1 – 5 V DC power supply&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;≥ 1 A (Pico + relays)&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#dae8fc;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=10;fontSize=12;spacingLeft=100;fillColor=#F8CECC;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1330" y="630" width="260" height="68" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c173" value="GND" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1330" y="636" width="80" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c174" value="+5V" style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fontSize=11;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#6c8ebf;strokeColor=#B85450;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1330" y="664" width="80" height="28" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c175" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#000000;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c51" target="c173"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c176" value="D1 Schottky&lt;br&gt;(SS14 / MBR120)" style="pointerEvents=1;html=1;shape=mxgraph.electrical.diodes.diode;verticalLabelPosition=top;verticalAlign=bottom;align=center;fontSize=10;fillColor=#000000;direction=west;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1225" y="668" width="60" height="20" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c177" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#B85450;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c174" target="c176"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c178" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#B85450;exitX=0;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c176" target="c52"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c179" value="+5V" style="rounded=1;arcSize=50;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F8CECC;strokeColor=#B85450;fontColor=#000000;fontSize=10;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1610" y="670" width="44" height="16" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c180" value="" style="endArrow=none;html=1;rounded=0;edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;strokeWidth=1.5;strokeColor=#B85450;exitX=1;exitY=0.5;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=0;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;" edge="1" parent="1" source="c174" target="c179"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"><Array as="points"><mxPoint x="1600" y="678.0"/></Array></mxGeometry></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c181" value="&lt;b&gt;Design notes (derived from the firmware)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;
1. &lt;b&gt;Relays&lt;/b&gt; (GP6-GP9, Output, default 0): the FW treats them as active HIGH and turns them all off at boot. Use a &amp;quot;high-level trigger&amp;quot; module or an NPN stage (BC337 + 1 kΩ base + 1N4007 flyback diode across the coil). Common active-low 5 V opto modules do NOT turn off reliably at 3.3 V.&lt;br&gt;
2. &lt;b&gt;Encoder&lt;/b&gt; (GP20 CCW / GP21 CW): internal pull-downs + IRQ on both edges → common C goes to &lt;b&gt;3V3&lt;/b&gt;. With a KY-040 module (10 k pull-ups to VCC and C to GND) the levels are inverted: remove the pull-ups or adapt the FW.&lt;br&gt;
3. &lt;b&gt;Buttons&lt;/b&gt; (GP18 Btn, GP19 EncoderBtn): internal pull-ups, close to GND, 50 ms SW debounce. Optional 100 nF to GND to reduce bouncing.&lt;br&gt;
4. &lt;b&gt;I2C&lt;/b&gt; at 100 kHz: I2C0 (GP16/17) → RTC 0x68, I2C1 (GP2/3) → OLED 0x3C. Internal pull-ups are enabled but insufficient: external 4.7 kΩ to 3V3 are required (the ZS-042 module already has them; R1/R2 only if the OLED module lacks them).&lt;br&gt;
5. &lt;b&gt;DS3231 ZS-042&lt;/b&gt;: power it from 3V3. With a non-rechargeable CR2032, remove the charging diode/resistor on the module.&lt;br&gt;
6. &lt;b&gt;RGB LED&lt;/b&gt; (GP13/14/15 PWM, wrap 255): higher duty = more light → &lt;b&gt;common cathode&lt;/b&gt; to GND. 220 Ω ≈ 5-7 mA per channel; tune for white balance.&lt;br&gt;
7. &lt;b&gt;UART0&lt;/b&gt; (GP0 TX / GP1 RX) 115200 8N1: stdio + AT command parser. Cross TX↔RX, 3.3 V adapters only.&lt;br&gt;
8. &lt;b&gt;Power&lt;/b&gt;: 5 V on VSYS through a Schottky (allows USB to be connected too). The solenoid valves are on a separate 24 VAC circuit, never referenced to logic GND." style="rounded=1;arcSize=2;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="790" width="1580" height="260" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
        <mxCell id="c182" value="" style="text;html=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="40" y="1075" width="1" height="1" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
